      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m not sure to understand.\n\nYou have a charger that can (supposedly) provide 2400 mA (I guess an Apple charger?), and the voltage drops below 4.5V before reaching that current?\n\nHow much current do you actually draw when you reach the 4.5V limit? What about if you set the limit to 4.096V?",
      "revId": "a09b5bdc68e59b785f8dc79bf19c3b0087fb4f2c",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "df48c328_1269d2bf",
        "filename": "board/zoombini/board.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 343,
      "author": {
        "id": 1125984
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-10-31T16:17:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The BC 1.2 detector chip (BQ24392) that we\u0027re using is configured a little strangely. Essentially, we get a binary signal that the charger is either a SDP or not (CDP, DCP, proprietary). We then assume the upper limit is 2400mA and ramp. The charger may not actually support drawing 2400mA, but much less. With one particularly bad charger, we saw Vbus drop to 4V at just 400mA.\n\nRegarding how much current we actually draw, I\u0027ll have to get back to you once I take a measurement.",
      "parentUuid": "d63e6f10_872c8a84",
      "revId": "a09b5bdc68e59b785f8dc79bf19c3b0087fb4f2c",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "350761b4_15277d2c",
        "filename": "board/zoombini/board.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 343,
      "author": {
        "id": 1001696
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-10-31T16:21:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Assuming your interpretation of this register is correct, it controls VBUS floor for \"HW ramp\" (eg. throttle ILIM once VBUS drops below this voltage). Our similar threshold for SW ramp is typically 4.6V (derived from BC1.2 min Vchg - tolerance). If we want HW ramp ramp to behave in a similar way, we should choose some floor close to 4.6V here?",
      "parentUuid": "d63e6f10_872c8a84",
      "revId": "a09b5bdc68e59b785f8dc79bf19c3b0087fb4f2c",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3b889003_e639651d",
        "filename": "board/zoombini/board.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 343,
      "author": {
        "id": 1125984
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-10-31T16:26:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The register takes values in 341.3mV steps. 4500 (and 4600) end up being set at ~4.439V. The next step is ~4.783V. I chose the lower value. Should I instead choose the higher one?",
      "parentUuid": "350761b4_15277d2c",
      "revId": "a09b5bdc68e59b785f8dc79bf19c3b0087fb4f2c",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c755dcaf_ec87fa29",
        "filename": "board/zoombini/board.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 343,
      "author": {
        "id": 1129199
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-10-31T16:30:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "On ISL9237 the limit was at 4.2V, and we left it to 4.096V on ISL9238, but 4.437V might also be ok (https://b.corp.google.com/issues/35586966), and we could just use that unconditionally and be done with it.\n\nFor non-proprietary chargers, we usually set the current limit at 2000/1000 (DCP/SDP), so I\u0027m not sure if setting it to 2400 all the time is a good idea... It\u0027s a pity the BC1.2 chip can\u0027t do better than this?!",
      "parentUuid": "350761b4_15277d2c",
      "revId": "a09b5bdc68e59b785f8dc79bf19c3b0087fb4f2c",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "54308895_ff0b749b",
        "filename": "board/zoombini/board.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 343,
      "author": {
        "id": 1125984
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-10-31T23:22:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think it\u0027s fine since we\u0027re ramping? On one DCP it\u0027s written \"output 5.2V \u003d 1.35A\". With a current probe, I measure ~1.42A from the charger. With a multimeter, I measure Vbus to be 4.501V. Changing the minimum input reference voltage to the default of 4.096V gives a negligible change in current.\n\nWith another DCP it\u0027s written \"5V \u003d 500mA\". With a current probe, I measure ~466mA and Vbus is 4.459V. Changing the minimum input reference voltage to 4.096V gives a current measurement of ~470mA.\n\nYeah, it\u0027s too bad that\u0027s all we get from the chip, but I think raising the minimum input voltage for the charger is a good step.",
      "parentUuid": "c755dcaf_ec87fa29",
      "revId": "a09b5bdc68e59b785f8dc79bf19c3b0087fb4f2c",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    }
